    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense, but if i present it that way some of them are gonna say we're basically just prioritizing political activism over our actual job. they'll argue that if there's a conflict between a social goal and maximizing profit, the profit should always win. is there any valid argument for why the fiduciary duty should stay strictly focused on the bottom line and nothing else?",
